Package: fhirtxencoder
Type: Package
Title: Encode Terminology Codes Using a FHIR Terminology Server
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("John", "Grimes", email = "John.Grimes@csiro.au",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation (CSIRO)",
           role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: Encodes terminology codes, such as SNOMED CT, into sparse
    multi-hot feature vectors suitable for use as machine learning features.
    The scope of the encoding is given as a FHIR ValueSet URI, which is
    expanded by a FHIR terminology server. Each code is represented by a row
    that carries the code itself, every concept within the scope that subsumes
    it, and optionally the concept properties reported by the server. A
    'recipes' step is provided for use within tidymodels pipelines.
